  "meta": {
    "title": "Helsinki · Rautatientori — open-data digital twin",
    "description": "Helsinki Central Station, the Cathedral and the Elielinaukio bus terminal as georeferenced IFC models on the OpenStreetMap city, with the Finnish Meteorological Institute’s air-quality and weather stations live. The terminal’s bays follow HSL’s buses in real time over MQTT: a bay lights up while a bus stands at it, green when its doors are open, with the line number above it.",
    "license": "CC BY 4.0 (this scene document). Data keep their own licences: see each layer.",
    "tags": [
      "helsinki",
      "digital twin",
      "open data",
      "IFC",
      "MQTT",
      "HSL",
      "FMI",
      "air quality"
    ],
    "place": {
      "name": "Rautatientori, Helsinki",
      "lat": 60.1712,
      "lon": 24.9416
    },
    "createdAt": "2026-10-10T01:00:00Z",
    "notes": [
      "The IFC files are illustrative models authored from public drawings, OpenStreetMap (ODbL) and the City of Helsinki LOD2 model; they are not surveys.",
      "Bus bays are matched to HSL stops by their platform number (GTFS, 2026-10-10). Bays 21, 27 and 31–36 have no HSL stop today and stay unlinked.",
      "The global terrain reads about 18 m above the Finnish N2000 heights here, so the models stand on the terrain’s surface rather than at their stated elevation."
    ]
  },
